@startuml journal-owner-trusted-checkpoint
' ============================================================================
' The journal owner's checkpoint after its switch to trusted successors
' (task 11946): DurableRSpaceAuthorityV1 in durable/rspace_authority.rs,
' checkpoint at :202-233, publish_captured at :235-289, reconcile at
' :291-333 and acknowledge_successor at :335-386.
' Model: formal/tlaplus/stack_safe_pda/RSpaceJournalPublicationOwner.tla
'   GREEN  #2E7D32  Ready: no pending publication, the base validates
'   BLUE   #1565C0  Captured: the journal captured under the write permit
'   AMBER  #EF6C00  RecoveryRequired: durable writes may have begun
'   PURPLE #6A1B9A  AwaitingAck: published, not yet acknowledged
'   RED    #C62828  Invalidated: the hot journal names another authority
'   GREY   #607D8B  notes
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.4
skinparam StateBorderColor #455A64
skinparam NoteBorderColor #455A64
hide empty description

title <b>The journal owner's checkpoint over trusted successors</b>\nthe owner keeps only a DurableAuthorityCoreV1, and only recovery runs a cold check

state "Ready" as Ready #C8E6C9
state "Captured" as Captured #BBDEFB
state "RecoveryRequired" as Recovery #FFE0B2
state "AwaitingAck" as Awaiting #E1BEE7
state "Invalidated" as Invalidated #FFCDD2

[*] -down-> Ready : from_view: the hot journal names the view's\nauthority; keep only the core (into_core)
Ready -down-> Captured : checkpoint: take the operation gate's write permit,\nvalidate the base, capture the pending journal
Captured -up-> Ready : <color:#2E7D32>empty batch: validate the base, drop the capture</color>\n<color:#2E7D32><b>no limit consulted, no hook, no cold check</b></color>
Captured -up-> Ready : <color:#C62828>refused before publication begins (mutation, transaction,</color>\n<color:#C62828>trusted bind or preparation): drop the capture; nothing is written</color>\n<color:#C62828><b>no hook, no cold check</b></color>
Captured -down-> Recovery : prepared under the wal limits;\nthe journal revalidated
Recovery -down-> Awaiting : <color:#1565C0>publish_trusted_incremental_v1 returns the successor</color>\n<color:#1565C0>core at the retained terminal</color>\n<color:#1565C0><b>trusted policy; 13 hooks; no cold check</b></color>
Recovery -right-> Recovery : the publication failed:\nkeep the capture, the permit\nand the retained terminal
Recovery -up-> Ready : <color:#EF6C00>reconcile: cold recovery selects the predecessor;</color>\n<color:#EF6C00>adopt its core, drop the capture</color>\n<color:#EF6C00><b>recovery, wal and admission limits; one cold check</b></color>
Recovery -down-> Awaiting : <color:#EF6C00>reconcile: cold recovery selects</color>\n<color:#EF6C00>the retained terminal</color>\n<color:#EF6C00><b>one cold check</b></color>
Awaiting -up-> Ready : <color:#6A1B9A>acknowledge_successor: pin the successor, acknowledge</color>\n<color:#6A1B9A>the journal, adopt the core, release the permit</color>\n<color:#6A1B9A><b>no limit consulted, no hook, no cold check</b></color>
Awaiting -right-> Awaiting : the pin or the acknowledgement\nfailed; a retry acknowledges once,\nwith no hook and no cold check
Ready -left-> Invalidated : the hot journal no longer\nnames the owner's authority
Invalidated -right-> Ready : the hot journal is restored\nto the owner's authority

note right of Recovery #ECEFF1
  <b>Exact terminal</b>
  The trusted publication retains its terminal
  before the swap. A successor at another slot,
  or a recovered slot that is neither the
  predecessor nor that terminal, is refused
  UnexpectedTerminal and stays here.
end note

note left of Invalidated #ECEFF1
  <b>Refusal, not repair</b>
  A checkpoint here is refused by the base
  validation before it captures anything.
end note
@enduml
